-- forfeit_password is no longer called only by the Google sign-in, so its
-- comment says who calls it now.

COMMENT ON FUNCTION public.forfeit_password(uuid) IS 'Sets the named auth user''s password to NULL, the state an account created through Google is in, so a password sign-in to it fails as invalid credentials; raises when no such user exists. NULL, never a random value: an unknown password is still a credential, and NULL is none; a password comes back only through a recovery link. Called through the service role wherever a credential must stop working: the Google claim, when a Google identity proves the address of an account whose address was never proven (the password may belong to someone who registered under another person''s address); and a parent moving a child to a mailbox or to parent sign-in, or withdrawing a credential that landed when the rest of that change failed. The account''s `email` identity is left in place. service_role only: it bypasses every check on who is asking.';
